As requested below i have ran the extract manually.  I have asked for this to be checked.

As you have mentioned BIU have received all of the PET data from 15th August which is great, however there are 69 patients that registered in ED on 14th August but they don’t have a discharge date/time so they remain as open episodes on our database and will effect Connolly’s PET times.

 

Normally the way around this would be to run a new extract going back to maybe 12th or 13th August to capture any changes made to these records. I would imagine the 69 patients do have a discharge date/time on your system but we haven’t received them which is due to the issue with the extract over the weekend. Currently the extract goes back 5 days but because the 14th August was last Thursday and the issue with the extract was resolved yesterday we actually missed out on any updates for that day.

 

If as a once of EMIS could set the parameters to 10 days for tomorrows file then that would capture the 14th August. I hope that makes sense but if you need to have a chat through then please do not hesitate to give me a call on the mobile number below.

