08/09/2025 15:22:42 - Konrad Siddons (Work notes)
CS1573246
Hello Zakar,

I am pleased to update we have found/come to a resolution for your case CS1573246.

To resolve this:

From the example A31 Inbound messages we have tracked and analysed, the data recorded in the DAD_Eventlogs table for them being processed indicates that the Symphony database was successfully updated, despite the Acknowledgement sent back to PAS being an AE (Error, not Failure).

It transpires that the issue arises when the number of DEP entries etc listed on the eView for a particular Attendance exceeds 75.
In this example the Attendance appears to be over several days probably accounting for some of these entries.

However, the vast majority of entries are Result Details Notification, all appearing to contain the same data.

We would advise reviewing the TIE settings to reduce or stop these repeated Notifications being sent to Symphony, to prevent this issue arising.

Many thanks

We are confident that this will resolve your issue, but if you find that this is not the case, please use the red 'Reject Solution' button so we are able to further investigate this issue for you.


Kind regards

Konrad

