21/10/2025 12:42:56 - Konrad Siddons (Work notes)
Guidance form Richard Henderson:

Print Template with which produces a file in a specified folder. Can't recall if there is another Windows Scheduled Task that copies the file elsewhere after that. Believe print template may also produce a WIF (text) file with some meta data from the attendance. Both files would be required for Evolve to import the PDF.

Run This:

SELECT  pjb_id, sf_name, pjb_name,  pjb_templatepath,Pjb_Path as OutputTo, pjb_WifTemplatePath as WIF,
CASE pjb_docformattype WHEN 1 then '.vpr'
when 2 then '.pdf'
when 3 then '.doc'
when 4 then '.tiff'
ELSE '' END as FileType,
CASE pjb_outputtype when 1 then 'printer'
when 2 then 'DocHistory File'
when 3 then 'Printer and DocHistory'
ELSE '' END as OutputType,
Pjb_DocFormatType, Pjb_OutputType, pjb_fileNameFormat
FROM  CFG_PrintJobs
inner join CFG_SymFolders on pjb_ParentId = sf_id
WHERE  pjb_deleted = 0 and pjb_id > 0 and Pjb_OutputType > 1  -- toggle this field to find jobs that produce files
order by Pjb_OutputType desc

