Gave Ashok (development) more data from the BlitzLock output.
 
He has been researching and mentions
When I dig some thing on Copilot it says to enable RCSI - Read Committed Snapshot Isolation on the database
It is currently set to off.
Apparently, it would require downtime with no SQL connections to change it.
 
Asked Richard Henderson (Implementations) view on this, is it something we can offer Leeds as possible remedy?
 
Richards reply:
its one of the newer isolation levels in SQL but a little out of my comfort area
 
