","Symphony","29/10/2025 14:17:52","","24",""
"CS1679127","University Hospital Southampton NHS Foundation Trust","4 - Low","29/10/2025 12:45:12","Closed","Symphony has removed NHS numbers for patients in eCamis. ","04/11/2025 17:27:52","system","Acute Care Symphony Support Level 1","Sheree Chadwick","30/10/2025 08:26:50 - Sheree Chadwick (Work notes)
These work notes are from a case back in 2024 - CS1182300.  There is nothing Symphony can do if they want the NHS numbers on Camis would have to update them.

This issue has now been raised as a design issue and passed to projects to test and implement a possible solution to remove the message segment with NHS number field from IAC messaging updates into Camis. This would avoid IAC messaging taking control of NHS number field, and Camis being sole owner of this data to disseminate to other systems.
Project ref 11809. Implementations should be in contact in due course.
Support workaround is as originally mentioned, exit the record giving enough time for the NHS number lookup to be completed and associated message to be received by Symphony without a lock on the patient record. Once NHS number is saved on Symphony record no issues can be caused by blank NHS number field in messaging.

