"CS1695294","University Hospital Southampton NHS Foundation Trust","3 - Medium","27/11/2025 09:55:26","Closed","Discharge summary stuck in the queue - unable to proceed","15/12/2025 12:10:05","system","Acute Care Symphony Support Level 1","Konrad Siddons","09/12/2025 15:46:48 - Lee Booth (Work notes)
Just to confirm, the full stops in the clinician notes are actually ASCII CHR code 7 which is BEL, an unprintable character classed as control character.
A full stop should be ASCII CHR code 46.
Ideally need to know how these got in the text. Dodgy keyboard, incompatible device?

