Email sent to Account Director Jmaes Heels:

Hi James
The above case was raised on behalf of Wendy Davies who is one the Design Team at the Trust.
This was not done via the usual Trust contacts, who are Lisa Thomas and Ria Woods, as both are currently on sick leave – Wendy made initial contact with our Primary Car support colleagues via online chat.

She is looking at designing a process for Symphony to send messages via the DAD Interface to their Integration Engine when patients attend the Emergency Department,  to feed a forthcoming Electronic Prescribing solution.

She has requested that we provide 'generic' documentation covering the DAD Interface and messaging.
However, since such documentation seems not to actually exist, probably due to the fact that Optum are generally responsible for development and implementation of the DAD and associated messaging, there is nothing suitable for us to hand over.
Moreover, as Wendy has little or no knowledge of Symphony, it would seem appropriate to support her efforts in a different way, to ensure her work leads to a realistic proposition.

To that end, having discussed this with Deployment colleagues, could you please raise an internal order to allow Deployment to reach out to Wendy and discuss what the actual requirements are, with a view to hopefully guiding the Customer towards requesting a quotation for Optum to design and implement any Symphony developments.

Please contact either Ceri or Rachel should you require any further information.

Kind regards
Konrad

