Email sent to James Heels following conversation about this case:

Hi James
As discussed in our earlier telephone conversation:

The above case was raised by Jay Duncan at the Trust, there having been work done locally with which I believe Optum have not been at all involved.
They are now seeking assistance with making their solution work:

"" BCUHB servers team are looking at a new version of RDS deployment for the EDs alongside Impravata SSO to enable 'follow me sessions' . so far its working as expected except for where E-Docs and scanned midas docs are concerned- , Adobe acrobat and Edge installed on all 10 RDS servers but not all of then are allowing viewing as expected , ... some work fine some show error: (attached)

Issue is that for the 10 RDS farms that are running against live and being tested against live (WM CDU we're using to rest away from live data areas). not all are functioning to enable the users to view or print e-docs, or midas documents at patient or attendance level... even tough all the RDS servers have Adobe pdf viewer and Edge on them (edge being the default for opening Word Docs in O365...). 
in TC and APPV deployments symph uses PCs applications to open these documents ... in RDS- these applications are run on the RDS server (as opposed to users PC) what we're finding is not 100% reliable to open any document in e-docs or Midas....
Be happy to set up a call with our servers team to demo and discuss...""

I believe this falls outside what Application Support are in a position to assist with, as it is not a failure of the existing Live or UAT system.

Could you please facilitate suitable resource(s) being made available to assist Jay, be it Server Team or Deployment colleagues, or a combination of both?
A assume there will be some cost to the Customer for provision of this assistance, which would of course need to be approved by The Trust prior to Optum becoming involved..

Kind regards
Konrad

