30/01/2026 15:09:28 - Gareth Evans (Work notes)
Been working with Carlos on this yesterday and today, trying to reproduce it on the test database. 

You should be able to get someone off the BRM grid by creating a TCI outcome and a request acknowledgement. But if there's a discharge on the clinic appointment, then we're getting an error: 'This DEP stage is not available for data collection (for this patient) because the conditional rules specified for triggering is default wait have not been met.'

When you record a discharge against a clinic appointment, you get asked for a TCI outcome, but presumably the process isn't recording the TCI details in a way that the BRM grid is looking for.

We've exhausted the ways we can think of to clear the appointment off the grid using tools available on the front end, so we'll need to remove it in SQL, in the same way that we do for the grey team.

