Subject: HSE – St. Columcilles - Daily Extract Amendment Required

Good Afternoon, 
 
The below has been received into the Support team. We have now resolved this support case as we deem this a potentially chargeable request; the customer has also been informed.  
 
Customer Support reference: CS1717231
Trust: HSE – St. Columcilles 
Customer contact name: Jeroen Verbruggen
Customer contact email: Jeroen.Verbruggen1@hse.ie
Customer contact number: 

Spoke to Jeroen and he's received a request from the HSE Business Intelligence Unit (BIU) to amend the existing daily PET data extract.

The extract was originally set up several years ago by Optum, and currently includes data points up to Point 15 (Gender) as outlined in the attached document 'New PET Data Points'. Jeroen is not aware who at Optum set this Extract up for them.

BIU would now like to include the remaining data points 16–21 in the report. Jeroen has advised BIU that this may involve additional work and could be chargeable. BIU has accepted this condition.

Points to be included in the Extract:

Point 16 - Triage Category - to be included
Point 17 - Triage Presenting Complaint - to be included
Point 18 - Discharge Diagnosis - to be included as they would like to see what the data this returns
Point 19 - Admitting Speciality - Not essential to be in the Extract
Point 20 - Reason for 24hr Breach - to be included
Point 21 - IHI - Not essential in the Extract

The Extract is located:
\\PNDCSYMSTCDBS20\SQL Server Agent\Jobs\EMIS - SDU Extract - LIU

The output of this extract is a daily CSV file located in:
\\PNDCSYMSTCDBS20\SQLJobLogs\

The SP is located:
\\PNDCSYMSTCDBS20\EMIS_SYM_StC_Replicated_Live\Programmability\Stored Procedures\spSDU_Extract_LIU

Advised Jeroen this case will be referred to the Commercial Team and the Account Manager.

Jeroen is happy to discuss these requirements further with you and provide clarification if needed. He is happy to go back to BIU if you require any additional details or to review the specifications.

Jeroen can be contacted on:
Jeroen.Verbruggen1@hse.ie

