13/02/2026 12:34:50 - Lee Booth (Work notes)
In Symphony, the Duty Clinician list is department?specific, not just controlled by the “System Duty Clinician = Yes” setting.
Key points you can send to the customer:

The Duty Clinician Management screen only lists clinicians who belong to that department and have “System Duty Clinician” set to Yes.
This means that a user will only appear in the Duty Clinician list for the department they are assigned to, not automatically for every site where they work.
Duty Clinicians are configured per department, and printed output is also based on department.
If a user’s Home Department is changed, they will stop appearing as a Duty Clinician for their old department.

So in the example with Lakshmi Ilavala:

If their Home Department is Doncaster, theybwill appear in the Duty Clinician list for Doncaster.
They will not appear in the Bassetlaw Duty Clinician list unless their staff record is also associated with Bassetlaw at the department level.

If Lakshmi needs to be Duty Clinician for both Doncaster and Bassetlaw, the organisation may need to review how their staff record is configured — specifically, whether they are associated with both departments in Symphony staff maintenance.

