13/02/2026 11:35:01 - Lee Booth (Work notes)
Easier to read investigation notes:

[code]
<p>Based on the <strong>Duty Clinician</strong> training docs and how printed output works, here are some structured investigation steps and guidance on whether to <strong>edit the history record</strong> or <strong>add a new duty period</strong>.</p>
<hr>
<h2>1. Confirm what <em>should</em> be happening</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Clarify the intended duty pattern with the site</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>Was the Consultant Nurse <strong>meant</strong> to stop being the duty clinician on <strong>31/12/2025</strong>, or should they have continued into <strong>2026</strong>?</li>
<li>This dictates whether the existing end date is:</li>
<li>a <strong>data entry error</strong>, or</li>
<li>a <strong>genuine historical end date</strong>.</li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><strong>Confirm impact on printed output</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>The documentation confirms that the <strong>Duty Clinician’s name appears on all printed output</strong> for attendances that started while they were on duty. </li>
<li>So if the duty period ended on <strong>31/12/2025 23:59</strong>, any attendances starting on or after <strong>01/01/2026</strong> will not include that clinician on discharge summaries.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2>2. Check configuration for the Consultant Nurse</h2>
<p>Do these checks <strong>before</strong> changing any dates:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Check ‘System Duty Clinician’ flag in Staff Maintenance</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>Open the staff record for the Consultant Nurse in SUM.</li>
<li>In <strong>Employment Details</strong>, confirm <strong>System Duty Clinician</strong> is set to <strong>Yes</strong> – this is required for them to be selectable as a Duty Clinician. </li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><strong>Check Home Department</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>Confirm their <strong>Home Department</strong> is still the relevant ED department.</li>
<li>The guide notes that if a duty clinician’s <strong>Home department is changed</strong>, their name will no longer appear on printed output for that department. </li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><strong>Confirm they haven’t lost SDC status</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>If the <strong>System Duty Clinician</strong> property has been changed from <strong>Yes</strong> to <strong>No</strong>, their name will also drop off printed output, even if duty periods are present. </li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2>3. Review current and future duty records</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Open the Duty Clinician Management screen</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>From <strong>Tools ? Duty Clinician</strong> to launch the <strong>Duty Clinician Management</strong> screen. </li>
<li>This screen shows <strong>current and future</strong> duty clinicians only. </li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><strong>Look for the Consultant Nurse</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>Check whether they are shown as:</li>
<li><strong>Current</strong> (green icon), or</li>
<li><strong>Future</strong> duty clinician (grey icon), or</li>
<li>Not present at all (only visible in <strong>History</strong>).</li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><strong>Open Duty Clinician History</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>With the relevant <strong>departmental folder</strong> selected in the Duty Clinician list, click <strong>History</strong> to open the <strong>Duty Clinician History</strong> screen. [\</li>
<li>Use the date range to include <strong>before and after 31/12/2025</strong> and click <strong>Show</strong> to pull all relevant records.</li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><strong>Locate the relevant history record</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>Identify the row where this Consultant Nurse’s duty period <strong>ends on 31/12/2025</strong>.</li>
<li>Confirm there are <strong>no overlapping duty periods</strong> for that department/speciality – the documentation specifies that <strong>duty periods should not overlap</strong>, otherwise a system warning is displayed. </li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2>4. Decide: <strong>Edit the history record vs Add a new duty period</strong></h2>
<p>From the documentation:</p>
<ul>
<li>The <strong>History</strong> screen allows you to <strong>edit the details of past clinicians</strong> or permanently delete them from history. </li>
<li>The <strong>Duty Clinician Management</strong> screen is the place to <strong>Add</strong> duty clinicians for current/future periods. </li>
</ul>
<h3>Option A – Edit the existing history record</h3>
<p>Use this if the Consultant Nurse was <strong>never meant</strong> to stop being duty clinician on 31/12/2025 (i.e. the end date is wrong).</p>
<p><strong>Steps:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>In <strong>Duty Clinician History</strong>, select the Consultant Nurse record that ends on <strong>31/12/2025</strong>.</li>
<li>Click <strong>Edit</strong>.</li>
<li>Adjust the <strong>End Date/Time</strong> to the correct date/time (e.g. extend into 2026, or remove the end where appropriate, respecting your local convention and ensuring there is still no overlap).</li>
<li>Save the record.</li>
<li>Re-check the <strong>Duty Clinician Management</strong> screen:</li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>The clinician should now appear as <strong>current</strong> (green icon) if the revised end date is in the future. </li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Pros:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Keeps a <strong>single continuous duty period</strong> if they were meant to be on duty throughout.</li>
<li>Historical attendances <strong>before and after 01/01/2026</strong> will align with one continuous duty period.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Use this when:</strong></p>
<p>The 31/12/2025 end date was <strong>entered in error</strong> and there was no real break in being duty clinician.</p>
<hr>
<h3>Option B – Add a new Duty Clinician period via Management screen</h3>
<p>Use this if the Consultant Nurse <strong>did</strong> stop being duty clinician on 31/12/2025 and is now being <strong>reinstated from a new date</strong> (e.g. from 01/02/2026).</p>
<p><strong>Steps:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>On the <strong>Duty Clinician Management</strong> screen, click <strong>Add</strong> to open the <strong>Set Duty Clinician</strong> screen. </li>
<li>In <strong>Duty Clinician</strong>, select the Consultant Nurse (they must have <strong>System Duty Clinician = Yes</strong> and correct department).</li>
<li>Set:</li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li><strong>Speciality</strong> as appropriate.</li>
<li><strong>Start Date/Time</strong> to the new date they should resume duty (e.g. <strong>01/01/2026 00:00</strong> or whatever the Trust agrees).</li>
<li><strong>End Date/Time</strong> as per the rota or leave blank if your local practice is to set open?ended then maintain later.</li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li>Save the record.</li>
<li>Confirm:</li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>No <strong>overlapping duty periods</strong> exist for the same department/speciality and time.</li>
<li>The clinician appears as <strong>current</strong> (green icon) if the start date is in the past and end date in the future. </li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Pros:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Preserves the <strong>original historical duty period</strong> ending 31/12/2025.</li>
<li>Clearly represents a <strong>break and later reinstatement</strong>, which can be important for reporting.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Use this when:</strong></p>
<p>The Consultant Nurse genuinely stopped being duty clinician at the end of 2025 and has now been <strong>re?assigned</strong> from a later date.</p>
<hr>
<h2>5. Validate that discharge summaries now show the clinician</h2>
<p>After you’ve made the change (Option A or B):</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Create a test attendance</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>Register a <strong>test patient</strong> in the same department.</li>
<li>Ensure the <strong>attendance start date/time</strong> falls within the new duty period.</li>
<li>Record the discharge as per normal.</li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><strong>Generate a discharge summary / DAD message</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>Produce the GP discharge summary or relevant output.</li>
<li>Confirm that the <strong>Duty Clinician’s name now appears</strong> where expected.</li>
<li>The docs state the name of the System Duty Clinician is available for inclusion on printed output for attendances starting while they were duty clinician. </li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><strong>If still missing:</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>Re-check:</li>
<li>System Duty Clinician = <strong>Yes</strong>. </li>
<li>Home Department correct. </li>
<li>Duty period dates/times truly cover the attendance start time.</li>
<li>If messaging uses DAD mappings, you may also want to cross?check any <strong>DAD / DAD mapping config</strong> around Duty Clinician (referenced in multiple Customer Release Notes where duty clinician outputs in DAD were fixed or adjusted). </li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2>6. Recommended answer to the original question</h2>
<p><strong>“To reinstate should we select edit to change the end date in duty clinician history or should we select add on duty clinician management screen?”</strong></p>
<p><strong>Guidance:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>If the Consultant Nurse <strong>should have remained duty clinician continuously</strong> past 31/12/2025  </li>
</ul>
<p>    ? <strong>Edit the existing history record</strong> to extend the end date (Option A), so your data accurately reflects one continuous period.</p>
<ul>
<li>If they <strong>stopped and are now being re?appointed</strong> from a new effective date  </li>
</ul>
<p>    ? Use <strong>Add</strong> on the <strong>Duty Clinician Management</strong> screen to create a <strong>new duty period</strong> (Option B), leaving the original historical end date intact.</p>
<p>Both approaches are supported by the product design: the <strong>History</strong> screen is explicitly intended to <strong>edit past clinician records</strong>, and the <strong>Management</strong> screen is for <strong>current/future configurations</strong>. </p>
<hr>
[/code]

