[code]
<p>Here’s a customer?ready explanation you can send back, plus a bit of background for you.</p>
<hr>
<h3>Suggested response to the customer</h3>
<p><strong>Short answer:</strong>  <br>It <em>is</em> possible to display RAT?related information in a flagged column on the Tracking Grid and to show the most recent entry, <strong>provided</strong> RAT completion is stored in a suitable field (typically a lookup or staff field) within the RAT/eNOTEs DEP. However, Symphony does not have a built?in “RAT eNOTEs completed by” column out?of?the?box – it relies on configuration.</p>
<p><strong>How this can be achieved</strong></p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Identify the RAT eNOTEs field to flag</strong>  </li>
</ol>
<p>    Your local Symphony System Manager will need to:</p>
<ul>
<li>Open DEP Config and locate the RAT/eNOTEs DEP and stage that represents RAT completion.</li>
<li>Identify the specific field that indicates RAT completion, for example:</li>
</ul>
<p>        <em>   A </em>lookup* value such as “RAT Completed – Yes”, or<br>        <em>   A </em>staff* field that records who completed the RAT.</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Configure the field as a Flagged Column on the Tracking Grid</strong></li>
</ol>
<p>    On the <strong>Flags</strong> tab for that field, they can:</p>
<p>    <em>   Set <strong>Tracking Grid Display</strong> to <strong>“Flag Column”</strong> (or </em>“Flag Column without icon”* if they want a text-only column).</p>
<ul>
<li>Set <strong>Flagged Item(s) Displayed</strong> to <strong>“Most Recent Record”</strong> so the Tracking Grid only shows the latest RAT entry rather than all historical ones.</li>
<li>Use <strong>Tracking Grid Values</strong> to control what is shown in the column:</li>
<li><strong>Field Value(s)</strong> – shows the actual value (e.g. staff initials, or “RAT Completed”).</li>
<li><strong>Mapped Value(s)</strong> – if required, they can map values (e.g. staff to initials or a specific code) via mappings and show those instead.</li>
</ul>
<p>    With this setup:</p>
<p>    <em>   The </em>Flagged Column (FC)* on the Tracking Grid will show the <strong>most recent RAT record</strong> for that patient.<br>    <em>   If a <strong>Staff</strong> field is used and mapped appropriately, the column can effectively show </em>who* most recently completed the RAT (for example, staff initials).</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Limitations to be aware of</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>Symphony can only display what is actually captured in a configured field. If there is <strong>no dedicated field</strong> that reliably records “RAT completed by [user]”, the system cannot infer this automatically.</li>
<li>The “Most Recent Record” option shows the last saved record for that flagged field; this will work for “most recently completed RAT” <strong>as long as</strong> clinicians are consistently recording RAT completion via that same field.</li>
<li>As with all configuration, this should be set up and validated in a <strong>Test</strong> environment first, then moved to Live once agreed.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>If this isn’t currently possible in your build</strong></p>
<p>If your current RAT/eNOTEs configuration does <strong>not</strong> include a specific field that can be flagged in this way (for example, no dedicated completion/staff field), then:</p>
<ul>
<li>It isn’t possible to show “who has most recently completed RAT eNOTEs” directly on the Tracking Grid with the current configuration.</li>
<li>Your local Symphony configuration team may wish to:</li>
<li>Introduce an appropriate field (e.g. a Staff field or dedicated lookup for RAT completion), and</li>
<li>Then configure that field as a flag as outlined above.</li>
</ul>
<p>We’d be happy to advise your local team on the safest way to implement this if needed.</p>
<hr>
<h3>Internal notes for you (not for the customer)</h3>
<ul>
<li>Flags support <strong>Lookup, MVDEF and Staff</strong> fields, and you can control:</li>
<li>Where they display (Patient Banner, Patient List, Tracking Grid Flag Column, etc.).</li>
<li>Whether you see <strong>all records, earliest, or most recent</strong>.</li>
<li>The key properties doing the work here are:</li>
</ul>
<p>    <em>   <strong>Tracking Grid Display</strong> ? set to </em>Flag Column*.<br>    <em>   <strong>Flagged Item(s) Displayed</strong> ? set to </em>Most Recent Record*.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Tracking Grid Values</strong> ? choose whether to show the raw field value or a mapped value (useful for staff initials / standard codes).</li>
<li>To truly show “who” completed RAT, the RAT process must have a <strong>Staff</strong> field (or equivalent) capturing the completer. If they only have free text or generic eNOTEs without a specific field, you can’t surface this cleanly on a single column.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
[/code]

