[code]
<p>Sure, here’s a shorter, cleaned?up version focused just on the key investigative routes, without all the extra narrative.</p>
<hr>
<h2>1. Confirm how WCP is launched</h2>
<p>From the TPWAL documentation:</p>
<ul>
<li>WCP is launched from Symphony via <strong>TPWAL</strong> acting as a proxy. [\[RLSE001210...Viewer CRN | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf</a>), [\[RLSE001124...ease Notes | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.9.1/RLSE0011242%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.9.1%20-%20Docman%20error%20handling%20Customer%20Release%20Notes.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.9.1/RLSE0011242%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.9.1%20-%20Docman%20error%20handling%20Customer%20Release%20Notes.pdf</a>)</li>
<li>Symphony (via DAD or another third?party system) sends a request to TPWAL; TPWAL <strong>encrypts the request using a configured key</strong>, builds a final WCP URL, and redirects the user into WCP with user + patient in context. [\[RLSE001210...Viewer CRN | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf</a>), [\[RLSE001124...ease Notes | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.9.1/RLSE0011242%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.9.1%20-%20Docman%20error%20handling%20Customer%20Release%20Notes.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.9.1/RLSE0011242%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.9.1%20-%20Docman%20error%20handling%20Customer%20Release%20Notes.pdf</a>)</li>
</ul>
<p>This means any break in the chain <strong>Symphony ? DAD ? TPWAL ? WCP</strong> can show up as a blank screen.</p>
<hr>
<h2>2. TPWAL checks (core for WCP issues)</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Check TPWAL is installed and running</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>TPWAL is a separate web application with its own site, app pool and database, used to launch third?party systems including <strong>Welsh Clinical Portal</strong>. [\[RLSE001210...Viewer CRN | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf</a>), [\[RLSE001124...ease Notes | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.9.1/RLSE0011242%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.9.1%20-%20Docman%20error%20handling%20Customer%20Release%20Notes.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.9.1/RLSE0011242%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.9.1%20-%20Docman%20error%20handling%20Customer%20Release%20Notes.pdf</a>)</li>
<li>Confirm on the TPWAL server that:</li>
<li>The TPWAL website exists.</li>
<li>The application pool is started.</li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><strong>Verify WCP configuration in TPWAL</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>In “About this release”, WCP is listed as one of the supported systems. [\[RLSE001210...Viewer CRN | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf</a>), [\[RLSE001124...ease Notes | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.9.1/RLSE0011242%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.9.1%20-%20Docman%20error%20handling%20Customer%20Release%20Notes.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.9.1/RLSE0011242%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.9.1%20-%20Docman%20error%20handling%20Customer%20Release%20Notes.pdf</a>)</li>
<li>In the TPWAL proxy configuration:</li>
<li>Check there is an entry for <strong>Welsh Clinical Portal / WCP</strong>.</li>
<li>Confirm the <strong>base WCP URL</strong> and any <strong>Password / EncryptionKey / IVKey / Secret Key</strong> fields are populated and match the agreed WCP setup for that site. [\[RLSE001210...Viewer CRN | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf</a>), [\[RLSE001124...ease Notes | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.9.1/RLSE0011242%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.9.1%20-%20Docman%20error%20handling%20Customer%20Release%20Notes.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.9.1/RLSE0011242%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.9.1%20-%20Docman%20error%20handling%20Customer%20Release%20Notes.pdf</a>)</li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><strong>Check for WCP?specific fixes / version</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>There is a specific fix “<strong>TPWAL – WCP – Encrypted URL needs to be updated</strong>”, which removed a hard?coded “?” to comply with the latest WCP specification. [\[RLSE001210...Viewer CRN | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf</a>), [\[RLSE001124...ease Notes | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.9.1/RLSE0011242%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.9.1%20-%20Docman%20error%20handling%20Customer%20Release%20Notes.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.9.1/RLSE0011242%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.9.1%20-%20Docman%20error%20handling%20Customer%20Release%20Notes.pdf</a>)</li>
<li>Confirm the customer’s TPWAL build is on a version that includes this fix (v1.0.1.0 or later as per the CRNs). [\[RLSE001210...Viewer CRN | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf</a>), [\[RLSE001124...ease Notes | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.9.1/RLSE0011242%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.9.1%20-%20Docman%20error%20handling%20Customer%20Release%20Notes.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.9.1/RLSE0011242%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.9.1%20-%20Docman%20error%20handling%20Customer%20Release%20Notes.pdf</a>)</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2>3. DAD / interface configuration checks</h2>
<p>The release notes state that for WCP:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>“A proxy has been created to receive requests from Symphony DAD or any other third?party system… The user is redirected automatically to the final URL which will take the user into the WCP system.”</strong> [\[RLSE001210...Viewer CRN | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf</a>), [\[RLSE001124...ease Notes | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.9.1/RLSE0011242%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.9.1%20-%20Docman%20error%20handling%20Customer%20Release%20Notes.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.9.1/RLSE0011242%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.9.1%20-%20Docman%20error%20handling%20Customer%20Release%20Notes.pdf</a>)</li>
</ul>
<p>Key checks:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>DAD outbound service</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>In Symphony’s DAD manager, confirm that the <strong>outbound service used to launch WCP/TPWAL</strong>:</li>
<li>Exists.</li>
<li>Is enabled.</li>
<li>Is not repeatedly erroring.</li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><strong>Endpoint alignment</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>Ensure the DAD service endpoint (URL) matches the <strong>TPWAL endpoint configured for WCP</strong> in the TPWAL proxy configuration. [\[RLSE001210...Viewer CRN | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf</a>), [\[RLSE001124...ease Notes | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.9.1/RLSE0011242%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.9.1%20-%20Docman%20error%20handling%20Customer%20Release%20Notes.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.9.1/RLSE0011242%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.9.1%20-%20Docman%20error%20handling%20Customer%20Release%20Notes.pdf</a>)</li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><strong>TPWAL logs / EventLogs</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>TPWAL uses a database to store configuration and logs; for other integrations (like ICE) it logs consumption requests and responses in tables such as <strong>EventLogs</strong>. [\[RLSE001210...Viewer CRN | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf</a>)</li>
<li>Check the TPWAL logs around the time you reproduce the issue to see:</li>
<li>Whether the WCP call is reaching TPWAL.</li>
<li>Any errors related to encryption, missing parameters, or URL building.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2>4. Next Action Menu / context checks</h2>
<p>The documents show similar interfaces (e.g. eCareLogic, Review) are launched from the <strong>Next Action Menu (NAM)</strong> with the active user and patient in context, using TPWAL as the proxy. [\[RLSE001210...Viewer CRN | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.10.2/RLSE0012104%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.10.2%20-%20RBAC%20changes%20for%20Web%20Viewer%20CRN.pdf</a>), [\[RLSE001124...ease Notes | PDF\]](<a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.9.1/RLSE0011242%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.9.1%20-%20Docman%20error%20handling%20Customer%20Release%20Notes.pdf"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/TPWAL/v1.0.9.1/RLSE0011242%20-TPWAL%20v1.0.9.1%20-%20Docman%20error%20handling%20Customer%20Release%20Notes.pdf</a>)</p>
<p>For WCP:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Check NAM mapping</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>Confirm the <strong>Next Action Menu item for WCP</strong> is configured to call the correct interface service / DAD request that ultimately targets TPWAL’s WCP endpoint.</li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><strong>Confirm patient context</strong></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>WCP and other viewers launched via TPWAL use patient identifiers (e.g. NHS number) passed in the query.</li>
<li>Ensure you test with a patient whose demographics/identifiers are valid in the local configuration.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2>5. Quick summary you can drop into the case</h2>
<p>For this customer, focus on:</p>
<ol>
