17/02/2026 12:03:49 - Lee Booth (Work notes)
[code]

<hr>
<h2>Investigation Guidance</h2>
<p><strong>Summary of issue</strong>  <br>Site reports that Next of Kin forename from PAS is being truncated in Symphony when there are multiple names in the PAS forename field, e.g. PAS NOK = <strong>“Anne and Simon”</strong>, Symphony NOK = <strong>“Anne”</strong> only.</p>
<p><strong>Likely cause</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Symphony and its HL7/DAD mappings are designed for <strong>one person per NOK record</strong>, with a single forename field mapped from the HL7 <strong>NK1-2 (Next of Kin Name)</strong> segment.</li>
<li>The interface mapping only uses the <strong>primary forename component</strong> (e.g. <code>NK1-2_2</code>) for the NOK forename in Symphony; additional names or multiple “entries” in the PAS forename field are not supported and are therefore not brought across.</li>
<li>If PAS is storing something like <strong>“Anne and Simon”</strong> as the NOK forename (i.e. multiple people in a single forename field), this is incompatible with Symphony’s model of a <strong>single person per NOK row</strong>, so Symphony will correctly show only the first forename.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Next steps for analyst</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>For example MRN <strong>936219</strong>, capture the <strong>inbound HL7 ADT message</strong> and check the <strong>NK1</strong> segment:</li>
<li>Confirm what is actually present in <code>NK1-2_2</code> (forename) and <code>NK1-2_3</code> (second forename).</li>
<li>If only “Anne” is already present in NK1, the truncation is occurring <strong>in PAS or the interface engine</strong>, not in Symphony.</li>
<li>Review the <strong>DAD Message Definition</strong> for NOK to confirm the mapping only uses <code>NK1-2_2</code> as the NOK forename field and does not concatenate multiple forename components.</li>
<li>Feed back to the site that current Symphony design and HL7 mapping <strong>do not support multiple people in a single NOK forename field</strong>; they should record separate NOK entries if they need more than one person.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
[/code]

