18/03/2026 11:53:36 - Konrad Siddons (Work notes)
Need to pass this issue over to Level 3 for further investigation and referral to Dev, as advised by Tracey McFarland who has investigated this with me:

In Live when Discharging Patients the system is prompting for the entry of Triage eNotes, though these are not Mandatory and there are no Pre-Requisites present in DEP Config for Discharge DEP.
Conditionality IS present in Discharge DEP to ensure all required DEPs have been completed - these do not include eNotes or Triage.

In UAT the config is set the same with no pre-requisites for Discharge, but the eNotes (and new RAT eNotes) are being prompted, though neither is Mandatory input.
Neither type of eNotes has any post-requisites or triggered stages in Live or UAT

Have replicated the issue in UAT.

.
The RAT process is a new abbreviated assessment process used in place of Triage.
Basically, a patient will be registered, see a Senior Decision maker (Clinician) straight away who will decide where the patient needs to go in the department and completes the RAT enotes DEP so may not get formally Triaged. The pt will then continue their journey and Clinician, Named Nurse, Xrays etc may still be recorded. Any ECDS reporting DEPs that have not been completed during attendance are set as pre or post reqs at the Ready DEP stage. Users can then click on Discharge and Left Department.

