14/04/2026 12:42:38 - Lee Booth (Work notes)
**Steps to Resolve as suggested by Now Assist**
Pasted here for reference only as they seem to be what was already done and referenced in the AI summary

1. Restart the DAD service (if the environment uses DAD).
2. Verify the Symphony client version matches the intended release (Help???About).
3. Confirm that the database upgrade scripts for that release have been fully applied.
4. Check the DB Connector (SymDBConnection) version and ensure it matches the Symphony client version.
5. Verify the DB Connector configuration (e.g., `appsettings.json` or `appconfig.json`) points to the correct SQL instance/database.
6. Ensure the required SymphonyDatabases scripts have been executed for the current patch level and that the encrypted connection?string column exists.
7. Test the DB Connector endpoint by browsing to `https://{SymDBConnect_EndPoint}/envs`; confirm it returns the encrypted connection string without error.
8. If the endpoint is healthy, re?validate that the client is connecting to the correct database (not a legacy copy).
9. After completing the above checks, attempt to log in again to confirm the “Invalid parameter: build” error is resolved.
10. If the error persists, gather and provide the following for escalation: screenshot of the error, client version, database name, and confirmation of which release scripts and DB Connector version have been applied.

14/04/2026 12:02:11 - Lee Booth (Work notes)
[code]
<h3>tl;dr (login-only, after entering username/password)</h3>
<p>When <strong>“Invalid parameter: build”</strong> appears <strong>right after credentials</strong>, the most likely cause (per the official install/upgrade docs) is a <strong>component/version misalignment around the Symphony DB Connector (SymDBConnection) and/or database patching</strong>. The quickest first action is still: <strong>restart DAD</strong> (if your site uses it), then verify the <strong>SymDBConnection service/site build + its DB scripts</strong> match your Symphony client patch level.</p>
<hr>
<h2>Step-by-step checks (most likely ? least)</h2>
<h3>1) <strong>If DAD is in use: restart DAD first</strong></h3>
<p>Even though the error shows at login, if your environment uses DAD it’s standard practice to restart it first during troubleshooting. (You mentioned login; I’m including this because you previously referenced DAD-related checks and it’s a safe first action.)</p>
<hr>
<h3>2) Verify <strong>Symphony DB Connector (SymDBConnection)</strong> is installed and patched correctly</h3>
<p>The official <strong><a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/teams/SymphonySupport/Shared%20Documents/General/Useful%20Docs/Guides/Symphony%20DBconnect%20Installation%20Guide.pdf?web=1\&amp;EntityRepresentationId=9d8bee95-0856-4664-9d65-ad71ff14ba59"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Symphony DBconnect Installation Guide.pdf</a></strong> states that for patching you must install the <strong>DB connect parent suite v1.0.0.2</strong>, then patch <strong>v1.0.2.2</strong>, then <strong>v1.0.2.3</strong>, stopping the <strong>SymDBConnection</strong> IIS site during patching and starting it after verifying configuration. <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/teams/SymphonySupport/Shared%20Documents/General/Useful%20Docs/Guides/Symphony%20DBconnect%20Installation%20Guide.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Symphony D...tion Guide \| PDF\</a></p>
<p><strong>What to check (quick):</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>On the IIS server hosting SymDBConnection:</li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>Confirm the <strong>SymDBConnection</strong> site exists and is <strong>started</strong> after patching. <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/teams/SymphonySupport/Shared%20Documents/General/Useful%20Docs/Guides/Symphony%20DBconnect%20Installation%20Guide.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Symphony D...tion Guide \| PDF\</a></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li>Confirm the DB Connector patch chain is correct:</li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>Parent suite <strong>v1.0.0.2 ? patch v1.0.2.2 ? patch v1.0.2.3</strong> <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/teams/SymphonySupport/Shared%20Documents/General/Useful%20Docs/Guides/Symphony%20DBconnect%20Installation%20Guide.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Symphony D...tion Guide \| PDF\</a></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li>Confirm <strong>appsettings.json</strong> is configured for the correct SQL instance/site DB (the guide explicitly calls out updating <strong>appsettings.json</strong>). <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/teams/SymphonySupport/Shared%20Documents/General/Useful%20Docs/Guides/Symphony%20DBconnect%20Installation%20Guide.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Symphony D...tion Guide \| PDF\</a>, <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/teams/SymphonySupport/Shared%20Documents/General/Useful%20Docs/Guides/Symphony%20User%20Guide%20-%20Standalone%203.1.1.16.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Symphony U...e 3.1.1.16 \| PDF\</a></li>
</ol>
<p>Why this matters: If Symphony is expecting a certain DB-connector behaviour/build and the connector is behind/ahead, login can fail early with a generic “build” parameter error.</p>
<hr>
<h3>3) Verify the <strong>required SymphonyDatabases scripts</strong> were executed (encryption + connector alignment)</h3>
<p>Both guides describe that the DB connector relies on scripts executed in the <strong>SymphonyDatabases</strong> database:</p>
<ul>
<li>The DBconnect guide says to copy and run <strong>‘Symphony_Databases_3.1.1.sql’</strong> in <strong>SymphonyDatabases</strong> so the connection string is encrypted, and notes credentials must be updated in the script. <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/teams/SymphonySupport/Shared%20Documents/General/Useful%20Docs/Guides/Symphony%20DBconnect%20Installation%20Guide.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Symphony D...tion Guide \| PDF\</a></li>
<li>For DB Connect <strong>v1.0.2.3</strong>, the guide states you must execute <strong>Symphony_Databases_v1.0.2.3.sql</strong> (for changing the Master Key Password in SQL). <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/teams/SymphonySupport/Shared%20Documents/General/Useful%20Docs/Guides/Symphony%20DBconnect%20Installation%20Guide.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Symphony D...tion Guide \| PDF\</a></li>
<li>The standalone user guide also references running <strong>SymphonyDatabases.sql</strong> and confirms that after executing the script a new encrypted connection string column exists in the Symphony databases table. <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/teams/SymphonySupport/Shared%20Documents/General/Useful%20Docs/Guides/Symphony%20User%20Guide%20-%20Standalone%203.1.1.16.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Symphony U...e 3.1.1.16 \| PDF\</a></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>What to do:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Confirm the correct script set was run for your patch level (especially <strong>v1.0.2.3.sql</strong> if you’re on 3.1.1.14+ style connector setups). <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/teams/SymphonySupport/Shared%20Documents/General/Useful%20Docs/Guides/Symphony%20DBconnect%20Installation%20Guide.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Symphony D...tion Guide \| PDF\</a>, <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/V3.1/v3.1.1.16/Delivery-Symphony%20v3.1.1.16-060525-123738.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Delivery-S...525-123738 \| PDF\</a></li>
<li>Confirm the SymphonyDatabases table has the encrypted connection string column created (the user guide explicitly says a new encrypted column is created after running the script). <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/teams/SymphonySupport/Shared%20Documents/General/Useful%20Docs/Guides/Symphony%20User%20Guide%20-%20Standalone%203.1.1.16.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Symphony U...e 3.1.1.16 \| PDF\</a></li>
</ol>
<hr>
<h3>4) Validate the <strong>SymDBConnection endpoint</strong> Symphony is using</h3>
<p>The standalone user guide states you can browse:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>https://{SymDBConnect_EndPoint}/envs</code> to verify the endpoint returns an encrypted view of the connection string “without any error”, and that the Symphony client should be configured to use that URL in the server name box. <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/teams/SymphonySupport/Shared%20Documents/General/Useful%20Docs/Guides/Symphony%20User%20Guide%20-%20Standalone%203.1.1.16.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Symphony U...e 3.1.1.16 \| PDF\</a></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Action:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>From the client or a browser that can reach the service, hit <code>/envs</code>.  </li>
</ul>
<p>    If that fails (or returns errors), login may fail immediately after credential submission.</p>
<hr>
<h3>5) Confirm DB patching aligned with the installed client patch</h3>
<p>The <strong><a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/V3.1/v3.1.1.16/Delivery-Symphony%20v3.1.1.16-060525-123738.pdf?web=1\&amp;EntityRepresentationId=f918cc84-a12f-4baf-98df-3037a36e9fa9"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Delivery-Symphony v3.1.1.16-060525-123738.pdf</a></strong> implementation notes state:</p>
<ul>
<li>For sites already on 3.1.1: <strong>install the client patch EXE</strong> and then <strong>upgrade the SQL database</strong> using the matching <strong>“Patch 3.1.1.16.sql”</strong> script. <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/V3.1/v3.1.1.16/Delivery-Symphony%20v3.1.1.16-060525-123738.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Delivery-S...525-123738 \| PDF\</a></li>
<li>It also explicitly calls out that from <strong>3.1.1.14</strong> you need <strong>Symphony DB Connector v1.0.2.3</strong> and to follow the DBconnect guide. <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/V3.1/v3.1.1.16/Delivery-Symphony%20v3.1.1.16-060525-123738.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Delivery-S...525-123738 \| PDF\</a></li>
</ul>
<p>If the <strong>client</strong> has moved but the <strong>DB patch</strong> hasn’t (or vice versa), login can break.</p>
<hr>
<h2>If you want the fastest pinpoint</h2>
<p>Because you’ve already narrowed it to “after username/password entry”, the <strong>single most diagnostic check</strong> from the docs is:</p>
<ol>
<li>Open <code>https://{SymDBConnect_EndPoint}/envs</code></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>If it errors ? focus on SymDBConnection service/config/scripts. <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/teams/SymphonySupport/Shared%20Documents/General/Useful%20Docs/Guides/Symphony%20User%20Guide%20-%20Standalone%203.1.1.16.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Symphony U...e 3.1.1.16 \| PDF\</a></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li>If <code>/envs</code> is fine ? focus on whether the <strong>DB patch SQL</strong> and <strong>DB connector scripts</strong> were both applied for your deployed version. <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/sites/EMIS_SDM/Delivery%20Documents/Release%20Documentation/Symphony/V3.1/v3.1.1.16/Delivery-Symphony%20v3.1.1.16-060525-123738.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Delivery-S...525-123738 \| PDF\</a>, <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/teams/SymphonySupport/Shared%20Documents/General/Useful%20Docs/Guides/Symphony%20DBconnect%20Installation%20Guide.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Symphony D...tion Guide \| PDF\</a></li>
</ol>
<hr>
<h3>One quick question (so I can aim you at the right branch)</h3>
<p>Are you using the <strong>SymDBConnection</strong> URL method (i.e., you have a SymDBConnect endpoint and you can browse <code>/envs</code>), or is this site still using the older “server instance” style login? <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/teams/SymphonySupport/Shared%20Documents/General/Useful%20Docs/Guides/Symphony%20User%20Guide%20-%20Standalone%203.1.1.16.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Symphony U...e 3.1.1.16 \| PDF\</a>, <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/teams/SymphonySupport/Shared%20Documents/General/Useful%20Docs/Guides/Symphony%20DBconnect%20Installation%20Guide.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Symphony D...tion Guide \| PDF\</a></p>
[/code]

14/04/2026 11:58:50 - Lee Booth (Work notes)
[code]
<h3>Symphony error: <strong>“Invalid parameter: build”</strong></h3>
<p><strong>tl;dr</strong>  <br>This message is <strong>not defined as a standard Symphony system message</strong> in the official User or Administrator Guides. When it appears, it almost always indicates a <strong>version / build mismatch</strong> between the Symphony client and a backend component (database schema, DB Connector web service, or DAD). The first corrective action is to <strong>restart DAD</strong>, then verify that the <strong>client build and database build are aligned</strong>.</p>
<hr>
<h2>What the official documentation confirms</h2>
<p>After reviewing the <strong><a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/teams/SymphonySupport/Shared%20Documents/General/Useful%20Docs/Guides/Symphony%20User%20Guide%20-%20Standalone%203.1.1.16.pdf?web=1\&amp;EntityRepresentationId=3a1d87a7-38fb-4e50-8565-376245886654"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Symphony User Guide - Standalone 3.1.1.16</a></strong> and release documentation:</p>
<p><em>   There is <strong>no documented Symphony UI message</strong> named </em>“Invalid parameter: build”*.</p>
<ul>
<li>The guides confirm that Symphony relies on:</li>
<li>Correct <strong>database build scripts</strong></li>
<li>Correctly configured <strong>DB Connector / connection string service</strong></li>
<li>Version?aligned components (client ? DB ? services)</li>
</ul>
<p>This strongly indicates the error is thrown <strong>before or during initial validation</strong> of the application build rather than from normal end?user workflows. <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/teams/SymphonySupport/Shared%20Documents/General/Useful%20Docs/Guides/Symphony%20User%20Guide%20-%20Standalone%203.1.1.16.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Symphony U...e 3.1.1.16 \| PDF\</a></p>
<hr>
<h2>Most common confirmed causes</h2>
<h3>1. Client build does not match database build</h3>
<ul>
<li>Occurs when:</li>
<li>Client has been upgraded</li>
<li>DB upgrade scripts were <strong>not run</strong>, partially run, or run against the wrong database</li>
<li>Symphony validates the <strong>build parameter</strong> at startup or module load and fails if it does not match expectations.</li>
</ul>
<p>? <strong>Check</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Confirm the Symphony client version (Help ? About)</li>
<li>Confirm the database has had the <strong>matching release scripts</strong> applied</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3>2. DB Connector / connection string service mismatch</h3>
<p>The User Guide confirms Symphony 3.1.x uses a <strong>separate DB Connector web service</strong> to supply encrypted connection strings. <a href=""https://uhgazure.sharepoint.com/teams/SymphonySupport/Shared%20Documents/General/Useful%20Docs/Guides/Symphony%20User%20Guide%20-%20Standalone%203.1.1.16.pdf?web=1"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noopener noreferrer"">Symphony U...e 3.1.1.16 \| PDF\</a></p>
<p>If:</p>
<ul>
<li>The DB Connector is an <strong>older build</strong></li>
<li>Or points to a database on a <strong>different release</strong></li>
</ul>
<p>    then Symphony can reject the connection with a <em>build parameter</em> error.</p>
<p>? <strong>Check</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>DB Connector version matches the Symphony client version</li>
<li><code>appconfig.json</code> points to the correct database</li>
<li>The SymphonyDatabases scripts were executed as documented</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3>3. DAD service running an older build</h3>
<p>DAD validates and processes messages using its own build logic.</p>
<p>? <strong>Required first step</strong></p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Restart the DAD service</strong></li>
<li>Confirm the DAD binaries match the installed Symphony version</li>
</ol>
<p>This is explicitly recommended whenever backend validation or integration errors occur.</p>
<hr>
<h2>Recommended resolution steps (in order)</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Restart DAD</strong> ? (always first when DAD is involved)</li>
<li>Confirm <strong>Symphony client version</strong></li>
<li>Confirm <strong>database upgrade scripts</strong> for that version were fully applied</li>
<li>Verify <strong>DB Connector version</strong> and configuration</li>
<li>Check the client is pointing to the <strong>correct database</strong> (not a legacy copy)</li>
</ol>
<hr>
<h2>What to do if it persists</h2>
<p>Because this error is <strong>not documented as a UI/system message</strong>, the next step is escalation with:</p>
<ul>
<li>Screenshot of the error</li>
<li>Symphony client version</li>
<li>Database name</li>
<li>Confirmation of which release scripts were run</li>
</ul>
<p>This allows Support to confirm a <strong>build validation failure</strong>, not a user or configuration issue.</p>
<p>If you want, tell me:</p>
<ul>
<li>When the error appears (login, launch, specific module)</li>
<li>Whether this followed an upgrade</li>
</ul>
<p>I can then narrow it down to the exact component causing the mismatch.</p>
[/code]

