I have been doing more investigation and research and found that possible issue with max text size 

SQL Server by using SQL Server Management Studio or Transact-SQL. The max text repl size option specifies the maximum size (in bytes) of text, ntext, varchar(max), nvarchar(max), varbinary(max), xml, and image data that can be added to a replicated column or captured column in a single INSERT, UPDATE, WRITETEXT, or UPDATETEXT statement. The default value is 65,536 bytes. A value of -1 indicates that there's no size limit, other than the limit imposed by the data type.

