A clear description of the Problem -
Some A31 messages are being acknowledged with AE status and it's not clear why. DAD_EventLogs says 'Saving Symphony Patient', but the Ack is sent back with the error status.

Time that the issue was first noticed; was anything specific that user or site (maintenance, upgrade etc) was doing at that point? -
First noticed in May, but I think it has been going on longer.

Details of any error messages appearing and their corresponding error log(s) -
The only error messages are the ACKs with AE status

Details on the user or user type reporting the issue -
Tommy is in IT

Machine specific or full hardware estate impacted e.g. Printing failure for all or one specific user/machine? -
It appears to be a data issue

What Investigation have you carried out / what knowledge based articles have you used - 
We've found the following messages in DAD_EventLogs that show the differences. Have a look at the rows with these del_ID's and their ACKs to get an idea: 
114124897, 106871032, 113853603. For contrast, these messages have been acknowledged correctly: 114283231, 114124925.

I've compared all these messages and can't find a pattern between the successful and unsuccessful messages. Comparing the five messages together, I've found no characteristics that are common only to one group or the other. All the referenced patients already existed on the system and had historical attendances. They all have valid GP details. For the first of the examples, I've taken every item that appears in the message and compared it to the frontend, and they match.

The only fields that are set as required on the DAD message definition are Hospital Number and NHS Number, and these appear correctly on all the patients.

Carlos and I have looked at this together, and we're stumped.

