Lee has checked the code 

looking at it, it doesn't appear to take the status in to account. The section is
        If Len(sPiNationalCode) <> 0 And Len(sPiGPPractise) <> 0 And Len(sPiGPPostCode) <> 0 Then
            'Search using national code, practise code and postcode
            If oPiGPs Is Nothing Then Set oPiGPs = New FWAssociations.FWGPs
            With oPiGPs
                .ConnectionString = sPiConnectionString
                .CurrentUserID = lPiCurrentUserID
                .FindForGPManagement sGPCode:=sPiNationalCode, sPractCode:=sPiGPPractise, sPosCode:=sPiGPPostCode
            End With
            If oPiGPs.Count = 0 Then Set oPiGPs = Nothing
        End If
 
 
dunno how much you understand code but it passes the ntional code, Practise code, and postdode to a function called 
 
FindForGPManagement
 
it does not pass a status (as the message won't know it anyway) and so the function doesn't use the status in the search
 
hence why when it looks for the Gp, Practice, Postcode combination, it finds more than 1

21/07/2026 12:41:59 - Sheree Chadwick (Work notes)
