10/07/2026 15:28:21 - Gareth Evans (Work notes)
Passing to PA's, Minimum data set below :-

A clear description of the Problem -
When HL7 messages from WPAS come in for patients in three specific practices, the GP information is removed from the patient, and users have to put the GP information back in manually. The practices are w93011, w95081 and w95073

Time that the issue was first noticed; was anything specific that user or site (maintenance, upgrade etc) was doing at that point? -
Not aware of any changes.

Details of any error messages appearing and their corresponding error log(s) -
In the DAD event log, after each of these messages there's an error: 'More than one GP was found that matches the criteria in the Symphony database.'

Details on the user or user type reporting the issue -
Chris is the System Manager

Machine specific or full hardware estate impacted e.g. Printing failure for all or one specific user/machine? -
For everyone — it's a data issue

Workaround offered or provided – users are re-entering GP details manually

What Investigation have you carried out / what knowledge based articles have you used - 
For each message that I've looked at, there's a very large number of GPPracticeAddressLink records for the practice. Some active, some inactive and some disabled. I think the answer might lie in the distinction between inactive and disabled.

A clear set of recreation steps -
Search DAD_EventLogs for messages containing one of the practice codes in question. You'll see the error message about more than one GP.

