[code]
<h2>Analyst Guidance</h2>
<p>Please complete the following targeted data checks to help identify the cause of the Error 91 in eView:</p>
<h3>Data Validation Checks</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Check all <strong>staff ID fields</strong> related to this attendance (e.g. DischargeCreatedByID, UpdatedByID, ArrivedCancelledBy):</li>
<li>Confirm none are <strong>0, null, or invalid</strong></li>
<li>Confirm associated staff details can be resolved correctly</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Review all <strong>relevant date fields</strong> (e.g. Created, Updated, Discharge dates):</li>
<li>Ensure no values are <strong>null, default placeholders, or malformed</strong></li>
<li>Confirm date sequencing is valid (e.g. updated date after created date where applicable)</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3>Data Integrity Focus</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Verify that all <strong>DEP lookups and related data objects</strong> are returning valid values</li>
<li>[ ] Check for any <strong>missing or incomplete data</strong> within the attendance record, particularly in:</li>
<li>Results</li>
<li>Requests</li>
<li>Outcome-related fields</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3>Assessment Summary</h3>
<p>Current indication is that this is <strong>not an application or environment issue</strong>, but a <strong>data-driven failure</strong>.</p>
<p>The underlying code does not fully handle null or missing values, so it appears likely that:</p>
<ul>
<li>A required field (DEP, lookup, or staff reference) is returning <strong>null or empty</strong>, and</li>
<li>This is not being validated before the system attempts to use it</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3>Working Hypothesis</h3>
<ul>
<li>Issue is consistent with:  </li>
</ul>
<p>  <strong>Single patient + eView + Error 91 ? null or unresolved DEP / lookup / staff reference</strong></p>
<hr>
<p>Please update with findings from the above checks so we can confirm the exact data point causing the failure or proceed with escalation if required.</p>
[/code]

