I have been logging calls on your call system, for monitoring purposes, as DAD is mainly being restarted in the Trust now. Today we have had to restart DAD twice, after adding extra RAM to the server, and the Trust have escalated this problem through Rachel, our EMIS project manager.

 

The call numbers raised so far are as follows:

 

CS1781968

CS1786243

CS1786278

CS1786626

CS1787187

CS1787222

CS1789867

CS1793655

CS1793711

 

Please could we discuss the DAD as a whole and can we include other parties

05/06/2026 11:30:33 - Janette Onen (Work notes)
emails from suzanne : 

Good Morning,

 

As you are aware, we are having issues with the DAD in East instance of Symphony.

 

As requested, Ali has been raising tickets every time the DAD goes down. 

 

Matt had suggested insufficient RAM so we increased it. However, the Dad went down again last night for 4 hours (12.42 was the last message and we didn't receive another until 4.43). 

 

We now have multiple Datix's due to DAD going down as it is a clinical risk, especially now that we have integrated Symphony with Patientrack and EPMA.  We cannot have this merely as a response to logged tickets every time DAD goes down as there are multiple failures every week. 

 

I would therefore appreciate it if someone could please escalate this to someone more senior within Optum and a meeting is set up to discuss how Optum will actively work with us to resolve this issue.

