11/06/2026 12:00:37 - Konrad Siddons (Work notes)
Email sent to Account Director. Angela Bath:

Hi Angela
Could you please arrange for a Quotation to be prepared and sent to the above trust.

The request is for Optum / Emis to undertake the unmerging of 2 Symphony  Patients whose records, including Demographic and historical ED Episode data were mistakenly merged at point in the past.
The data in its present form represents some degree of Potential Patient Clinical Risk.

As has been pointed out to the Trust, there is  no facility available within Symphony or at the disposal of ourselves in Support to unmerge patients, as you are requesting - hence the Stand Alone Patient Merge (SAPM) utility offering the user several opportunities to abort any merge being carried out before finally committing, to prompt them to be absolutely sure what they are attempting to do is valid.

""RLQ0601675 / NHS 4305412780 EL & RLQ0856363 / NHS 608 036 9397 ERL  has been merged on Symphony at some point but they are two different patients""

The nature of the work required deems it habitually chargeable and having to be carried out by appropriate Development colleagues.
The precise level of resource and time required is dependant upon how much data and of what type requires unknitting.

When completed, could the Quotation please be sent to Rachel Price at the trust:

rachel.price@wvt.nhs.uk

If and when the quote is accepted, please could the task then be forwarded to Development for the work to be scheduled and undertaken?

Many thanks.



Best regards
Konrad Siddons

