"CS1794930","Betsi Cadwaladr University Healthboard","4 - Low","08/06/2026 16:20:02","On hold","e-docs issue with digital photos","28/07/2026 13:52:57","Shazad.Ishaque@emishealth.com","Acute Care Symphony Support Level 1","Shazad Ishaque","14/07/2026 15:48:57 - Lee Booth (Work notes)
This issue is caused by high?resolution digital images exceeding the memory limits of the Symphony v2 e?DOCs component (FWePICsUI), where images are fully loaded into memory during upload; evidence in CS1794930 - e-docs issue shows original photos >10MB (16–24MP) load successfully for the first image but trigger “Out of memory” and “Failed to save to JPG” errors when a second image is added, confirming cumulative memory exhaustion rather than permissions or SQL issues, and attempts to “reduce size” by converting JPG to BMP actually worsened memory usage due to lack of compression; analysts should advise users to reduce image resolution (not just file size), use compressed JPG format, and avoid BMP/PNG for large images, as this is a known limitation of legacy image handling rather than a defect in environment or configuration.

