"CS1796075","Swansea Bay University Health Board","3 - Medium","10/06/2026 12:22:28","Resolved","Error message when discharging and trying to book clinic appointment","19/06/2026 11:47:13","konrad.siddons@emishealth.com","Acute Care Symphony Support Level 1","Konrad Siddons","19/06/2026 10:51:38 - Konrad Siddons (Work notes)
Summary of issue and findings for passing over to Level 3 for Problem to be raised:

REPLICATION STEPS
Select Patient Attendance from eView which needs to be discharged for follow-up appointment at MIU Physio Clinic.
Select Discharge DEP.
Discharge Date defaults to today's date.
Enter all required Discharge details and set Discharge Follow Up field to 'MIU Physio'.

ANALYSIS
On entry of this data the system should then offer the Clinic Diary for the required data and time of the required appointment to be selected.
However, in this case the system prompts with a System Message if the current day's session is Disabled, prompting the reason for this based on the comments present on the corresponding ClinicInstance table entry.
On selectin OK, the system should then offer the Clinic Diary for an appointment to be selected.
However, if the next ClinicInstance entry is also set to Disabled, the following error appears:

DATETIME: 16-Jun-2026 14:36:59|| DESCRIPTION: Object variable or With block variable not set|| SOURCE: FWClinicApptUI|| COMPONENT: FWClinicApptUI|| ERRORNO: 91|| PROCEDURE: ClinicApptUI.GetNextEnabledInstance|| CODEBLOCK: Error while generating the next enabled clinic.|| USFMESSAGE: || APPLICATION: Symphony Version 2|| ATTENDANCENO: MOED-22-000009-1|| PATIENTID: 117178|| PCNAME: WA-WNSY02DAD001|| SERVERNAME: sbuwedssqlext_p.cymru.nhs.uk|| LOGGEDUSER: symphonyadmin|| SITE: Swansea Bay LIVE|| BUILDNO: 2.39.1.19|| OS: Version 6.2 Build 9200 || DBTYPE: || DBVERSION: 2.39.1|| MDACVERSION: 6.3||

CONCLUSION
On investigating further it appears that this issue / error arises when there are 2 or more consecutive Clinic Sessions which are set to cln_disabled = 1; today's session and the next scheduled session.

This is believed to be due to a code fault rather than a Stored Procedure - Support are therefore unable to make any changes to rectify this issue.

Raised in yesterday's PTT and was agreed that a Problem Record should be raised and the issue referred to Development for a fix / patch / inclusion in future release.


WORKAROUND
Users are having to select a different discharge outcome and book appointments directly in the clinic and bypass booking via the Discharge DEP.

