17/06/2026 10:30:31 - Sheree Chadwick (Work notes)
Checked in HA failover events and can see that last night around 8.15 a failover was done back to 01 from 02.

ran the below and found that the tpwal db had not been written to since,

SELECT TOP (1000) [LogId]
,[LogSystem]
,[Environment]
,[LogType]
,[LogMessage]
,[CreatedOn]
FROM [EMIS_TPWAL].[dbo].[EventLogs]
where logsystem = 12
order by CreatedOn desc

On last failover to 02 the tpwal db had lost the master key and ran the below script so ran this on 01 and postcoder is now working again.

""*ServerName*"" and under the EMIS_TPWAL Database. USE [EMIS_TPWAL];
GO
OPEN MASTER KEY DECRYPTION BY PASSWORD = 'f00tmanAct1vated';
ALTER MASTER KEY ADD ENCRYPTION BY SERVICE MASTER KEY;
CLOSE MASTER KEY;
GO

