09/07/2026 10:05:24 - Lee Booth (Work notes)
[code]
<h2><strong>Case Summary: Symphony Login Failure After Location Changes</strong></h2>
<h3><strong>Initial Report</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>First call received at approximately <strong>21:20</strong>.</li>
</ul>
<p><em> User reported: </em>“Symphony not working.”*</p>
<ul>
<li>Site had a <strong>similar issue earlier (01:30)</strong>, where the <strong>SQL server had gone offline</strong>.</li>
<li>At that time, the user was advised to contact their <strong>internal IT team</strong>.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3><strong>Follow-up &amp; Symptoms</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>Second call received just before <strong>22:00</strong>.</li>
<li>User confirmed IT had checked the server and it was <strong>online</strong>, indicating a <strong>different issue</strong>.</li>
<li>Upon investigation, the issue occurred when <strong>attempting to log in to Symphony</strong>.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3><strong>Errors Observed</strong></h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Initial Error:</strong></li>
</ol>
<p>   <em> </em>“Bad file name”* when retrieving icons</p>
<ul>
<li>Typically indicates a <strong>corrupt image file</strong></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><strong>Secondary Error:</strong></li>
</ol>
<p>   <em> </em>“Object variable or With block variable not set”*</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Error 91</strong></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3><strong>Initial Troubleshooting</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>Attempted to:</li>
<li>Identify and remove any <strong>suspected corrupt image files</strong> (based on previous similar incidents)</li>
<li>Outcome:</li>
<li><strong>No resolution</strong></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3><strong>Investigation &amp; Findings</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>Recent <strong>system changes identified</strong>:</li>
<li>New locations added earlier in the week</li>
<li>Modification made to one location around the time the issue occurred (suspected <strong>EEMAC8</strong>)</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>Further investigation confirmed:</li>
<li>The system was attempting to save a <strong>corrupt icon file</strong> to the following path:  </li>
</ul>
<p>    <code>\herefordshire.gov.uk\wvt\Ascribe\ERRORS\CorruptIcons2\</code></p>
<ul>
<li>This <strong>network location was unavailable</strong>, causing the login failure</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3><strong>Resolution</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>Updated the <strong>file path</strong> in the <strong><code>systemproperties</code> table</strong>:</li>
<li>Changed from:</li>
<li><code>\herefordshire.gov.uk\wvt\Ascribe\ERRORS\CorruptIcons2\</code></li>
<li>To:</li>
<li><code>C:\</code></li>
<li>Result:</li>
<li>? Symphony successfully loaded and login issue resolved</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3><strong>Root Cause</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Unavailable network path</strong> for storing corrupt icon files</li>
<li>Triggered after recent <strong>location configuration changes</strong></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3><strong>Key Takeaways / Training Notes</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>“Bad file name” error during login may indicate:</li>
<li>Corrupt image/icon files <strong>or</strong></li>
<li>Issues with the <strong>configured storage path</strong>, not just the files themselves</li>
<li>If removing suspected corrupt images does not resolve:</li>
<li>Verify the <strong>availability and accessibility of the configured file path</strong></li>
<li>Check recent:</li>
<li><strong>Location changes</strong></li>
<li><strong>System configuration updates</strong></li>
<li>Validate paths stored in:</li>
<li><strong><code>systemproperties</code> table</strong></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3><strong>Suggested Next Steps (Preventative)</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>Ensure network paths used for error handling are:</li>
<li>Accessible</li>
<li>Monitored for availability</li>
<li>Consider using a <strong>local fallback path</strong> where appropriate</li>
<li>Review processes for <strong>location/configuration changes</strong></li>
</ul>
[/code]

